                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a dead game where 50-75% are multibox bots and pvp is just mutlibox or groups of 5+ people with 15 year old accounts griefing beginner ships for zero profit essentially aside from making them quit the game. Since they made the safe zone, many accounts will quit before they ever leave it and not become targets in the world. So instead the new accounts that do leave it instantly are screwed because the game's pvp these days is just 15 year old accounts gate camping beginner zones where there's less and less beginners to kill because many don't leave the safe zone before they quit. So less and less players will be in regular zones as the people who get out of the safe zone keep getting griefed endlessly by participation trophy players who can't get a kill any other way even after playing for 15 years.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1793390272,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1793390272,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 13,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5856451392173767,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hey there Zhorn,\n\nLeaving the starter region and getting caught by an experienced gang on your first trips out is a rough introduction, and it is understandable that it soured the game for you.\n\nA few points for anyone reading this. In the starter systems, [url=https://support.eveonline.com/hc/en-us/articles/203209712-Rookie-Griefing]all forms of rookie griefing are prohibited[/url], and if you see it happening it can be reported through the support website. Outside them, EVE is a sandbox where conflict is always possible, but character age matters far less than it seems: in Tech I frigates and cruisers, new pilots can reach the same skill levels as 15+ year old characters within a short time, and fit, tactics and awareness decide most fights.\n\nThe best counter to gate camps is not flying alone. Groups are strong because they are groups, and the in-game corporation finder has New Pilot Friendly and New Pilot Focused filters to help new players find people who will fly with them, scout routes and teach them how to spot and avoid camps. Many players who blow up a newcomer are also happy to explain what went wrong if you strike up a conversation afterwards.\n\nWe do, however, understand that EVE Online is not for everyone, but we thank you for playing and reviewing EVE Online.\n-The EVE Online Dev Team",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1793619078,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
